          "id": "code-ml-19-2-ch19_2_sklearn",
          "title": "Scikit-Learn 1.9: TruncatedSVD Sparse CSR (Randomized vs ARPACK) & IncrementalPCA Streaming",
          "language": "python",
          "filename": "19_2_sklearn_truncated_incremental_svd.py",
          "code": "import numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import IncrementalPCA, PCA, TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfTransformer\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(1922)\n\n# 1) Simulasi Matriks Term-Document Sparse (1000 dokumen x 2000 kata, kepadatan ~2.2%)\nn_docs, n_vocab, n_topics = 1000, 2000, 6\nrows, cols, vals = [], [], []\ntopic_blocks = np.array_split(np.arange(n_vocab), n_topics)\nfor doc_i in range(n_docs):\n    main_t = doc_i % n_topics\n    # Kata dari topik utama + sedikit kata noise lintas kosakata\n    w_main = rng.choice(topic_blocks[main_t], size=32, replace=False)\n    w_noise = rng.choice(n_vocab, size=12, replace=False)\n    chosen = np.unique(np.concatenate([w_main, w_noise]))\n    counts = rng.integers(1, 6, size=len(chosen))\n    rows.extend([doc_i] * len(chosen))\n    cols.extend(chosen.tolist())\n    vals.extend(counts.tolist())\n\nX_counts = sparse.csr_matrix((vals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n_docs, n_vocab), dtype=np.float64)\nX_tfidf = TfidfTransformer(norm=\"l2\").fit_transform(X_counts)\n\ncsr_kb = (X_tfidf.data.nbytes + X_tfidf.indices.nbytes + X_tfidf.indptr.nbytes) / 1024.0\ndense_kb = (n_docs * n_vocab * 8) / 1024.0\ndensity_pct = 100.0 * X_tfidf.nnz / (n_docs * n_vocab)\n\n# Perbandingan TruncatedSVD Randomized vs ARPACK (Lanczos eksak) langsung di atas CSR\nsvd_rand = TruncatedSVD(n_components=10, algorithm=\"randomized\", n_iter=5, random_state=42).fit(X_tfidf)\nsvd_arp = TruncatedSVD(n_components=10, algorithm=\"arpack\", random_state=42).fit(X_tfidf)\n\nsv_rel_diff = float(np.max(np.abs(svd_rand.singular_values_ - svd_arp.singular_values_) / svd_arp.singular_values_))\n\nprint(\"=== 1. TruncatedSVD pada Matriks TF-IDF Sparse CSR (1000 x 2000) ===\")\nprint(f\"Kepadatan nnz         = {density_pct:.2f}% ({X_tfidf.nnz} entri bukan-nol)\")\nprint(f\"Memori CSR vs Dense   = {csr_kb:.1f} KB (CSR) vs {dense_kb:.1f} KB (Dense PCA) -> Hemat {dense_kb/csr_kb:.1f}x!\")\nprint(f\"Proyeksi Produksi 1M x 100K (nnz 0.1%): ~1.2 GB (CSR) vs 800.0 GB (Dense -> OOM!)\")\nprint(f\"EVR Top-6 (Randomized)= {svd_rand.explained_variance_ratio_[:6].sum():.4f} | (ARPACK)= {svd_arp.explained_variance_ratio_[:6].sum():.4f}\")\nprint(f\"Max RelDiff Top-10 SV (Randomized n_iter=5 vs ARPACK) = {sv_rel_diff:.2e}\")\n\n# 2) IncrementalPCA untuk Streaming / Out-of-Core Data (Partial Fit per Mini-Batch)\nn_stream, d_stream, k_inc = 1200, 50, 5\nW_lat = rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=(d_stream, 5))\nX_stream = rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=(n_stream, 5)) @ W_lat.T + rng.normal(0.0, 0.5, size=(n_stream, d_stream))\n\npca_full = PCA(n_components=k_inc, svd_solver=\"full\").fit(X_stream)\nipca = IncrementalPCA(n_components=k_inc, batch_size=150)\nfor start in range(0, n_stream, 150):\n    ipca.partial_fit(X_stream[start : start + 150])\n\n# Ukur keselarasan subruang (subspace overlap: 1.0000 = identik sempurna)\noverlap = float(np.linalg.norm(pca_full.components_ @ ipca.components_.T, \"fro\") ** 2 / k_inc)\nrecon_full = float(np.mean((X_stream - pca_full.inverse_transform(pca_full.transform(X_stream))) ** 2))\nrecon_inc = float(np.mean((X_stream - ipca.inverse_transform(ipca.transform(X_stream))) ** 2))\n\nprint(\"\\n=== 2. Streaming Out-of-Core: Full PCA vs IncrementalPCA (8 batch x 150) ===\")\nprint(f\"Full PCA        | CumEVR={pca_full.explained_variance_ratio_.sum():.5f} | Recon MSE={recon_full:.5f}\")\nprint(f\"IncrementalPCA  | CumEVR={ipca.explained_variance_ratio_.sum():.5f} | Recon MSE={recon_inc:.5f}\")\nprint(f\"Subspace Overlap ||V_full V_inc^T||_F^2 / k = {overlap:.6f} (1.0000 = identik!)\")",
          "expectedOutput": "=== 1. TruncatedSVD pada Matriks TF-IDF Sparse CSR (1000 x 2000) ===\nKepadatan nnz         = 2.19% (43816 entri bukan-nol)\nMemori CSR vs Dense   = 517.4 KB (CSR) vs 15625.0 KB (Dense PCA) -> Hemat 30.2x!\nProyeksi Produksi 1M x 100K (nnz 0.1%): ~1.2 GB (CSR) vs 800.0 GB (Dense -> OOM!)\nEVR Top-6 (Randomized)= 0.0536 | (ARPACK)= 0.0536\nMax RelDiff Top-10 SV (Randomized n_iter=5 vs ARPACK) = 3.71e-02\n\n=== 2. Streaming Out-of-Core: Full PCA vs IncrementalPCA (8 batch x 150) ===\nFull PCA        | CumEVR=0.95198 | Recon MSE=0.22308\nIncrementalPCA  | CumEVR=0.95198 | Recon MSE=0.22308\nSubspace Overlap ||V_full V_inc^T||_F^2 / k = 1.000000 (1.0000 = identik!)",
          "actualOutput": "=== 1. TruncatedSVD pada Matriks TF-IDF Sparse CSR (1000 x 2000) ===\nKepadatan nnz         = 2.19% (43816 entri bukan-nol)\nMemori CSR vs Dense   = 517.4 KB (CSR) vs 15625.0 KB (Dense PCA) -> Hemat 30.2x!\nProyeksi Produksi 1M x 100K (nnz 0.1%): ~1.2 GB (CSR) vs 800.0 GB (Dense -> OOM!)\nEVR Top-6 (Randomized)= 0.0536 | (ARPACK)= 0.0536\nMax RelDiff Top-10 SV (Randomized n_iter=5 vs ARPACK) = 3.71e-02\n\n=== 2. Streaming Out-of-Core: Full PCA vs IncrementalPCA (8 batch x 150) ===\nFull PCA        | CumEVR=0.95198 | Recon MSE=0.22308\nIncrementalPCA  | CumEVR=0.95198 | Recon MSE=0.22308\nSubspace Overlap ||V_full V_inc^T||_F^2 / k = 1.000000 (1.0000 = identik!)",
          "explanation": "Membandingkan efisiensi memori CSR vs dense PCA pada matriks TF-IDF, memvalidasi kesesuaian TruncatedSVD(algorithm='randomized', n_iter=5) terhadap ARPACK eksak, serta menguji IncrementalPCA partial_fit pada aliran mini-batch.",
