          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef halko_rsvd_audit(A, k: int, p: int = 4, q: int = 2, seed: int = 42) -> tuple[float, float, bool]:\n    A = np.asarray(A, dtype=float)\n    n, d = A.shape\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    l = min(k + p, min(n, d))\n    Omega = rng.standard_normal((d, l))\n    Q, _ = np.linalg.qr(A @ Omega, mode=\"reduced\")\n    for _ in range(q):\n        Qz, _ = np.linalg.qr(A.T @ Q, mode=\"reduced\")\n        Q, _ = np.linalg.qr(A @ Qz, mode=\"reduced\")\n    B = Q.T @ A\n    Ut, s_r, Vt_r = np.linalg.svd(B, full_matrices=False)\n    Uk, sk, Vtk = Q @ Ut[:, :k], s_r[:k], Vt_r[:k, :]\n    A_hat = (Uk * sk[None, :]) @ Vtk\n    rsvd_err = float(np.linalg.norm(A - A_hat, \"fro\"))\n    _, s_ex, _ = np.linalg.svd(A, full_matrices=False)\n    opt_err = float(np.sqrt(np.sum(s_ex[k:] ** 2)))\n    excess_ratio = (rsvd_err - opt_err) / opt_err\n    sv_k_rel = abs(float(sk[-1] - s_ex[k - 1])) / float(s_ex[k - 1])\n    q_orth_ok = bool(np.linalg.norm(Q.T @ Q - np.eye(l), \"fro\") < 1e-10)\n    return (round(excess_ratio, 4), round(sv_k_rel, 4), q_orth_ok)\n```"
