          "code": "import numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import NMF, TruncatedSVD\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(1932)\n\n# Simulasi 450 keranjang belanja ritel x 25 kategori produk (5 persona belanja aditif)\n# Persona 0: Bayi/Ibu (0..4), Persona 1: Kopi/Kantor (5..9), Persona 2: Masak Rumah (10..14),\n# Persona 3: Olahraga/Sehat (15..19), Persona 4: Elektronik/Aksesori (20..24)\nn_baskets, n_items, n_personas = 450, 25, 5\ntrue_persona = rng.integers(0, n_personas, size=n_baskets)\nX_basket = np.zeros((n_baskets, n_items), dtype=float)\nfor i in range(n_baskets):\n    p_main = true_persona[i]\n    p_sec = (p_main + rng.integers(1, n_personas)) % n_personas\n    X_basket[i, p_main * 5 : (p_main + 1) * 5] += rng.poisson(lam=3.5, size=5)\n    # 35% keranjang membawa sedikit campuran persona sekunder (aditif!)\n    if rng.uniform() < 0.35:\n        X_basket[i, p_sec * 5 : (p_sec + 1) * 5] += rng.poisson(lam=1.0, size=5)\n    X_basket[i] += rng.poisson(lam=0.12, size=n_items)\n\ndef block_purity(H_mat: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Seberapa murni tiap komponen menangkap 1 blok persona 5-produk sejati.\"\"\"\n    purities = []\n    for row in np.abs(H_mat):\n        block_sums = [float(np.sum(row[b * 5 : (b + 1) * 5])) for b in range(5)]\n        purities.append(max(block_sums) / (sum(block_sums) + 1e-12))\n    return float(np.mean(purities))\n\nsvd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=5, random_state=42).fit(X_basket)\nnmf_cd = NMF(n_components=5, init=\"nndsvda\", solver=\"cd\", beta_loss=\"frobenius\", max_iter=400, random_state=42).fit(X_basket)\nnmf_kl = NMF(n_components=5, init=\"nndsvda\", solver=\"mu\", beta_loss=\"kullback-leibler\", max_iter=400, random_state=42).fit(X_basket)\nnmf_sp = NMF(\n    n_components=5, init=\"nndsvda\", solver=\"cd\", beta_loss=\"frobenius\",\n    alpha_W=0.02, alpha_H=0.02, l1_ratio=0.80, max_iter=400, random_state=42\n).fit(X_basket)\n\nprint(\"=== Perbandingan Faktorisasi Keranjang Ritel (450 Keranjang x 25 Produk, 5 Persona) ===\")\nprint(\"Model                     | Negatif (%) | Sparsity H (<1e-2) | Kemurnian Persona | Frob Recon Err\")\nprint(\"-\" * 98)\nfor name, H_m, X_hat in [\n    (\"TruncatedSVD (rank=5)\", svd.components_, svd.inverse_transform(svd.transform(X_basket))),\n    (\"NMF CD (Frobenius)\", nmf_cd.components_, nmf_cd.transform(X_basket) @ nmf_cd.components_),\n    (\"NMF MU (KL-Divergence)\", nmf_kl.components_, nmf_kl.transform(X_basket) @ nmf_kl.components_),\n    (\"NMF CD + L1 Sparse\", nmf_sp.components_, nmf_sp.transform(X_basket) @ nmf_sp.components_),\n]:\n    neg_pct = 100.0 * float(np.mean(H_m < -1e-6))\n    Hn = H_m / (np.max(np.abs(H_m), axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-12)\n    sp_pct = 100.0 * float(np.mean(np.abs(Hn) < 0.05))\n    purity = block_purity(H_m)\n    frob = float(np.linalg.norm(X_basket - X_hat, \"fro\"))\n    print(f\"{name:25s} | {neg_pct:10.1f}% | {sp_pct:17.1f}% | {purity:17.4f} | {frob:14.2f}\")",
          "expectedOutput": "=== Perbandingan Faktorisasi Keranjang Ritel (450 Keranjang x 25 Produk, 5 Persona) ===\nModel                     | Negatif (%) | Sparsity H (<1e-2) | Kemurnian Persona | Frob Recon Err\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTruncatedSVD (rank=5)     |       40.0% |               4.8% |            0.3564 |          90.01\nNMF CD (Frobenius)        |        0.0% |              80.0% |            0.9774 |          90.05\nNMF MU (KL-Divergence)    |        0.0% |              80.0% |            1.0000 |          90.21\nNMF CD + L1 Sparse        |        0.0% |              78.4% |            0.6978 |         115.66",
          "actualOutput": "=== Perbandingan Faktorisasi Keranjang Ritel (450 Keranjang x 25 Produk, 5 Persona) ===\nModel                     | Negatif (%) | Sparsity H (<1e-2) | Kemurnian Persona | Frob Recon Err\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTruncatedSVD (rank=5)     |       40.0% |               4.8% |            0.3564 |          90.01\nNMF CD (Frobenius)        |        0.0% |              80.0% |            0.9774 |          90.05\nNMF MU (KL-Divergence)    |        0.0% |              80.0% |            1.0000 |          90.21\nNMF CD + L1 Sparse        |        0.0% |              78.4% |            0.6978 |         115.66",
