          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef nmf_mu_frobenius_step(X, W0, H0, n_iter: int = 120, eps: float = 1e-9) -> tuple[float, float, bool, float]:\n    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=float)\n    W = np.asarray(W0, dtype=float).copy()\n    H = np.asarray(H0, dtype=float).copy()\n    loss_init = 0.5 * float(np.sum((X - W @ H) ** 2))\n    prev = loss_init\n    monotone = True\n    for _ in range(n_iter):\n        H *= (W.T @ X) / (W.T @ W @ H + eps)\n        W *= (X @ H.T) / (W @ H @ H.T + eps)\n        curr = 0.5 * float(np.sum((X - W @ H) ** 2))\n        if curr > prev + 1e-7:\n            monotone = False\n        prev = curr\n    Hn = H / (np.max(H, axis=1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n    h_sparse = float(np.mean(Hn < 0.05))\n    return (round(loss_init, 4), round(prev, 4), bool(monotone), round(h_sparse, 4))\n```"
